					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "RANDOM\n\nThe Random node allows you to generate floats, integers and booleans with randomized values.\nTo generate a value, the node will need a trigger or event change.\n\nYou set the range of the generated value by adjusting the min and max parameters.\nYou can set the type (boolean, integer, float, float2, float3 or float4) in the node panel.\n\nThe values will be generated using a seed.\nSetting a seed will make sure that the same random values are generated every time.\nThis is mostly useful when instancing the node, but most of the time you will leave this at 0.\n\nPrecision allows you to set how precise\/detailed the generated value is.\nMost of the time you don't need a float with ten decimals. \n\nDistribution allows you to set the distribution between uniform or normal(Gaussian).\nWe'll dive into how this works in the distribution example."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 355.4239501953125,
					"width": 846.968994140625,
					"x": 183.920684814453125,
					"y": -704.73126220703125
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
