						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 3: RANDOM GRADIENT & SEEDS\n\nIn this example we've increased the instance count to 25.\nThis allows us to generate a gradient.\nDo note that each instance of the random node needs its own seed.\nIf we would use the same seed for each instance, we would get the same result on multiple channels.\n\nAlso note that in the node panel and multi editor(ctrl+click the \"multiple\"  box on the node) you can randomize the seeds."
					}
