					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 6: SMOOTHING RANDOMNESS\n\nIn some cases you might want to smooth the random output you are getting from the Random node.\nThere are two solutions for this, both demonstrated in the example below.\nThe first solution is to add a Smooth node after the Random node, this will interpolate between the values over a given duration.\nThe second solution might be to use the Perlin Generator node instead.\nWhich one you should use depends on the look you are going for.\nIn this example the top rectangle is smoothed Random and the bottom is Perlin Generator."
					}
				},
